# Version Rule

Update the project version every time a user message results in one or more project modifications.

## Format

`XX.XX.XX` — starting version: `00.01.00`

## Increment

For each completed modifying user message, increase by `00.00.01` once.

Examples:

- `00.01.00` → `00.01.01`
- `00.01.98` → `00.01.99`
- `00.01.99` → `00.02.00`
- `00.99.99` → `01.00.00`

When a section reaches `99`, the next increment rolls over into the section to the left.

## Change-set scope

- Multiple modifications in one user message = **one** version increment.
- Do not increment multiple times for changes within the same user message.
- Messages that only read, explain, or review (no file changes) do not increment.

## Storage

- Canonical version: root `VERSION` file.
- Also keep `application/config/version` in `project.godot` identical.
- Show the version in the debug menu and in a corner of the title screen, so screenshots and recordings show which build they came from.
- Include the version in every `docs/PROGRESS.md` entry and phase report.
- Before finishing, verify the current version is updated everywhere it is stored, displayed, or referenced.
